  "risks": [
    "ECR app layers/manifests, audit objects and GitHub Actions/artifact storage may incur fees; no workload restoration or 50 USD hard spending guarantee.",
    "One docker push may cause multiple ECR layer/manifest requests and Docker-internal transport retries. A failed/unknown push is never reissued by the operator; partial uploads/images/audits may remain.",
    "The fixed backend-read token is read only in the cloud job, used only with GitHub official API; AWS/OIDC credentials and bounded artifacts enter memory/runner-private storage. Never forward credentials to signed blob hosts or commit raw tokens/logs.",
    "Catalog registration uses the broad existing owner config once; whole config enters memory and PostgreSQL/provider logs may retain statements or credential material. Temporary owner membership writes occur even in independent inspection transactions; creator ADMIN is not removed.",
    "Publication, A/B registration and independent inspection are not one atomic operation. A may publish/register while B remains absent; COMMIT ACK unknown is not made successful by a matching readback, and no INSERT/push/grant/cleanup is automatically retried.",
    "Only two immutable release records are in scope. Existing document, status, revocation or ownership conflicts stop; no UPDATE/DELETE, role/Secret recreation, schema replay or business/binding writes.",
    "No product/API/current database or full-media persistence proof is created by catalog policy adoption. Required runtime facts/persistence remain a later separately approved initial activation prerequisite.",
    "Unknown code entry, CI, current role/registry/environment state or actual derived manifest prevents an executable approval SHA; this planning document itself grants no reads or writes.",
    "Approval includes publishing the exact non-secret review data on main and later closing that bootstrap config. These commits may trigger ordinary no-AWS CI; no source or daily-runtime change is permitted.",
    "The local source credential/helper, cloud OIDC session, fixed backend token, signed original ZIP and registry proofs enter their bounded processes/disks. GitHub metadata and Account ID/ARN appear in review/audit records. Never save credentials, signed download URLs or raw private configuration.",
    "Independent catalog inspection still performs temporary role-membership writes. Exact preexisting A may be recognized only by the existing immutable full-document equality check; unknown INSERT/COMMIT must never become a successful write merely because a later read matches.",
    "Current live DB compatibility, image persistence, initial binding and runtime remain unproved/disabled; catalog registration cannot waive those gates or authorize restore. No resources are auto-stopped by the fact/write deadline.",
    "New operations require startup by the fixed latestStart and finish before writeBefore or the per-stage deadline. A long GitHub queue or approval delay can stop after partial publication; do not extend, rebuild or replay."
